      "hypotheses": "One finite complete uncoloured labelled-forest space on nonempty inputs; ordinary completion P onto absorbing genealogy space Z, and source kernels fixing Z. PSD statement requires every individual form to contract under every stated source B and ordinary exp(tQ); differentiable statement requires E:V→R continuously differentiable on signed vectors, strict convexity on Z, and both contraction inequalities for every signed vector.",
      "conclusions": [
        "Every individually contractive PSD form annihilates range(PB-P); no jointly faithful such family exists for the strict fair-cell quartet contrast. An arbitrary faithful family reduces to a finite one in finite dimension.",
        "A globally differentiable common energy under the specified signed hypotheses forces PB=P and hence is excluded by the same contrast. Simplex-only smoothness is insufficient.",
        "For merger-only uncoloured stochastic K, E_eta(x)=(sum r_f|x_f|)^2+eta||x||², 0<eta<=1/4, is a faithful strongly convex common contraction and a finite maximum of positive-definite quadratic forms. Only their maximum contracts. eta is cap independent; the finite family/state space depends on the cap."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "No assertion for coloured routing kernels retaining assignments.",
        "The energy charges ordinary mergers too; neither a target-relative nonnegative defect nor equality characterization, finite I bridge, or weak-cell exclusion follows.",
        "No retraction of the original fixed-Hilbert result or scoped chronological energy."
      ],
      "review_involvement": "Laplace lane supplied the follow-through; Sol independently audited it but had previously reviewed the reset obstruction and did not supply the envelope construction. Lead independently checked displayed bounds and accepted scope. All are coordinated agent reviews, not external or human certification."
    },
